÷3÷Working_with_Browser_Module_Files÷Working with Browser Module Files÷The Open Watcom Browser
îWorking_with_Browser_Module_Files

ìModule file, in Browserì ìBrowser, working with module filesì Once a Browser database file is loaded, you might want to edit the list of modules originally used to create the database file.  Editing the list of modules allows you to temporarily remove modules from the database or add modules to the database.  For example, you may decide that you only want to browse a particular module or set of modules or you may have forgotten a module when the database was originally created.

Theïbï Modulesğ menu item in theïbï Fileğ menu allows you to view the list of module files that make up the current database file.  From this list you can perform the following functions on the module files:

Òc
Ó Add

Ó Remove

Ó Disable

Ó Enable
Ô

courier12°c°brow3.bmp°helv10
ïibïFigure 3.ğïibïğïbï On the Modules dialog, you can add, remove, disable, and enable module files.ğ
´
÷4÷Adding_a_Module_File÷Adding a Module File÷The Open Watcom Browser
îAdding_a_Module_File

ìBrowser, add Module fileì ìModule file, add in Browserì

Ê
Ì(1)
¹ïbï Chooseğïbï Modulesğ from theïbï Fileğ menu.

This opens theïbï Modulesğ dialog for the current database file.  This dialog lists all module files that make up the database file.  Each module file has a check box.  An X in this box indicates that the module file is enabled.  The Browser browses only the enabled module files.

Ì(2)
¹ïbï Click on theğïbï Addğ button in theïbï Modulesğ dialog.

This opens theïbï Select Module File(s)ğ dialog where you choose the module files to add to the current Browser file.

Ì(3)
¹ïbï Select the module filesğ to add to the Browser file and click onïbï OK.ğ  Select multiple module files by holding the Shift key while you click on the desired files.

Clicking on OK closes theïbï Select Module File(s)ğ dialog and adds the selected module file to the database file.  Each module file in the module list has a check box.  When added, this check box is marked with an X, indicating that the module file is enabled.

Ì(4)
¹ïbï Continue with steps 2 and 3ğ until you have added all desired module files to the component list.

Ì(5)
¹ïbï Click onğïbï OKğ in theïbï Moduleğ dialog.

This closes theïbï Modulesğ dialog and updates the database file.
Ë
´
